WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.800
Lina Haddad: Thanks for making the time, Omar. Can you tell me how you usually do your weekly grocery shop?

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:13.100
Omar Khalil: Sure. I order on Thursday night from my phone, because Friday morning is the only time I'm home to receive it.

3
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:21.900
Omar Khalil: The problem is the delivery window. They give me a two hour slot and the driver still shows up late, so I lose half my morning waiting.

4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.000
Lina Haddad: What do you do while you wait?

5
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:34.200
Omar Khalil: Honestly I just sit by the door. I can't go to the gym, I can't take the kids out. It feels like the app owns my Friday.

6
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.900
Lina Haddad: When was the last time that happened?

7
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:47.600
Omar Khalil: Last week. The order said 9 to 11 and it came at 11:40. Nobody called. I had to message support three times.

8
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.400
Lina Haddad: Have you tried other apps for this?

9
00:00:52.900 --> 00:01:02.300
Omar Khalil: I tried two others. One was cheaper but the vegetables were bad. I'd pay a bit more if I could just see where the driver is.

10
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.000
Lina Haddad: Why does seeing the driver matter so much to you?

11
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:15.800
Omar Khalil: Because then I can plan. If I know he's twenty minutes away I can finish breakfast. Right now it's a guessing game.

12
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.200
Lina Haddad: That's really helpful. Anything else you'd change?

13
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:27.400
Omar Khalil: Substitutions. When something is out of stock they swap it without asking me, and half the time it's a brand my kids won't eat.
